<title>LITHUANIA: SNORAS BANK OPENS REP OFFICE IN MINSK.</title>
<headline>SNORAS BANK OPENS REP OFFICE IN MINSK.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lithuania's Snoras bank said on Friday that it had opened its first foreign representative office in Minsk, the capital of Belarus, and was eyeing expanding into other CIS countries and the Czech Republic.</p>
<p>&quot;Today we opened our first foreign representative office in Minsk,&quot; the chairman of Snoras Bank, Raimondas Baranauskas, told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;We want to open other representative offices in Prague, Moscow, St.Petersburg, Kiev and Almaty this year,&quot; Baranauskas added, but declined to mention any specific dates.</p>
<p>Snoras Bank, the seventh largest bank in Lithuania, is active in CIS soft currency and debt markets.</p>
<p>--Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom +370 2 22 35 17</p>
</text>
